B.cRS=new A.p("bubbles",B.V,'Opt-in chat-bubble row styling: { byColumn, selfValue, example }. Rows whose byColumn value matches the resolved selfValue (a literal, or a token like $playerId / $rowId / $selected:<table>) render end-aligned + tinted ("me"); everything else (including an unset selfValue token) renders start-aligned + neutral ("them"). Absent entirely -> the plain ListTile row, unchanged. Optional `example: { ids: [...], label, hideLabel, chipLabel, hiddenFromSetting, onHide }` marks demo-content rows (house-design-rules.md rule 10): each listed row id gets a small "example" chip (chipLabel, localizable), a slim label+divider (label, localizable) renders once above the first such row with a Hide action (hideLabel + onHide, an action spec), and when the named `hiddenFromSetting` board setting resolves truthy (\'1\'/\'true\') those rows are dropped from the list entirely.',B.f,null)
